WEBVTT

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.330
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.430
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.660
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.760
(Yami, the Hat and the Book traveler)
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:35.700
I had always believed
that what I saw before me...

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:42.500
...was the only truth there was.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:50.330
But now I know
there isn't just one world.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:59.800
There are a thousand worlds called
"if" and I don't know which way to turn.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.760
I want to see you but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.900
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:16.660
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.600
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:26.600
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.560
I'll keep searching for you.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.200
It's okay, just make it.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:53.260
I'm sure anything you
make will taste good.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:15.000
These hotcakes represent
Hatsumi's very own angelic love.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.560
I love you very much!

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:21.860
I hope you
understand that because I...

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.230
What's wrong, sis?

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.430
Lilith
We just teleported
but it's unusually slow.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.830
I feel exhausted now, like
a princess with a weak heart.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.560
Why don't you take
control for a change?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:54.960
Oh, that's right, I'm wearing
the hat now, I almost forgot.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.230
How could you forget?

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.560
How many tens of thousands of years
has it been since you last wore it?

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.630
Not sure.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.630
I'm not good about
remembering that type of stuff.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.800
We can discuss it
much, much later.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:17.260
In this library, every world in the
universe is sealed inside its own book.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.260
Eve, the librarian, and
Lilith are returning back here.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.730
Finally, the day has come.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.860
It's great to be home!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.160
Do you know how much
I've suffered because of you?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.730
Suffered?

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.200
That hurt.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.330
Of course, it was meant to hurt.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.460
Did you really have
to hit me with your fist?

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.200
It was my palm!

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.560
What did I do wrong?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.700
Your very existence, itself, is wrong!

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.930
I don't really mean that but...

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:17.700
Still.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.430
Sis.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.230
I had lonely days, too.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.660
Hey, Eve.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.400
You won't call me
big forehead girl?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:56.330
Big head! Big head!
Big head! Big head! Big head!

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.330
I've travelled to so many
worlds since I met with Lilith.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:09.100
It seems like they were all
real but... also like dreams.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.530
I just took a bath...

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.600
...but in another world, there
was a me who didn't take a bath.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.630
That's what Lilith
said once, didn't she?

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.700
That day, a me who
met Youko on the train that night...

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:39.060
...and a me who didn't meet her.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.900
In another primitive world,
there was a me who met Quill...

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.760
...and a me who didn't.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.860
On a desert island,
there was a me who met Milka...

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.830
...and a me who didn't.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.530
In ancient Japan, there was
a me who met princess Fuji...

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.630
...and a me who didn't.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.730
In the future on a spaceship,
there was a me who met Leila...

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.930
...and a me who didn't.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.900
In the strange space gardens,...

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.260
...there was a me who met with
Tamamo no Mae and a me who didn't.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:22.000
Did Hatsumi ever
exist in this world or not?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.830
Does Hatsumi only exist in
my mind and my memories?

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.600
It's the same even
if she was never here.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:57.630
At this very moment, she is
nowhere so it's all the same.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.530
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:14.560
Thank you.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.460
What is this!?

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.160
What's with the hotcakes?

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.300
I didn't order these!

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.760
Is it the restaurant breakfast special?

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.160
Take them away!

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:28.000
Is there something
wrong with our service?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.460
But, but!

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:33.600
Eve's hotcakes are known
throughout the entire universe!

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:39.400
They're unforgettable, so dream-like,
they melt-in-your-mouth!

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.230
Sis!

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.030
That's too much!

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:50.260
Hazuki said they
were simply delicious.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.830
Sorry.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:05.830
I wonder what Hazuki is doing now?

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.500
Hazuki's not here.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.800
You sure you've got the right book?

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:27.400
Of course, me and Hazuki
grew up together in this book!

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.100
Then she hasn't
returned to her original world?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.760
I guess so.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.160
I think the other books in
the series should all be here.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.500
You know very
well where they are!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.860
Because I've been taking
care of this place for a long time.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.730
I meant that to be sarcastic.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.230
I want to hold her.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.330
I want to... hold her.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.560
Is there anything wrong, Hatsumi?

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.660
It's your birthday tomorrow, isn't it?

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:30.900
Oh right, you'll be 16!

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.200
That calls for a party.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.030
Please come straight
home tomorrow, alright?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.800
I hope you have a
good sleep tonight.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:53.000
What does that "bye-bye" mean?

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.760
It should have been "good night".

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.500
To Hatsumi Azuma

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:09.400
I love you so much,
how could you be so cruel!

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:20.530
I... I'm so sorry.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.260
I'll go get some
medicine and a bandage!

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:45.300
Hatsumi... can
you make a sexy pose?

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:50.860
Turn around, don't be shy!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.430
Come closer,
that's great Hatsumi!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.560
If I open this door,
something terrible will happen.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:42.330
For some reason, I know that.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:34.730
I am sorry, Hatsumi.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.100
Hazuki.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:06.230
Hatsumi, you can speak!?

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:10.700
Hatsumi?

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:05.730
So soft.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:35.430
Can you just hold me
like this for a while?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:51.160
What you really need...

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.530
...you will never be able to
catch it no matter how hard you try.

00:16:56.600 --> 00:17:02.230
Because you already have
it inside of you to begin with.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.360
I must've fallen
asleep in the empty room.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:25.730
Oh?

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:47.560
Why do I remember this taste?

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:59.730
Mother, did you
make these hotcakes?

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:13.600
It's strange...

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:20.160
...how do I know that the baby
I'll have one day will be a girl?

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.730
St. Feminine Girls School

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:06.300
And, how do I
already know her name?

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:36.000
You've travelled so
many different worlds, right?

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.660
Tell me about the most
interesting world you found.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:42.160
The most interesting? Hmm...

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:46.060
Well, what are you
gonna do next, sis?

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.730
What should I do?

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.730
I feel like it's time
to go on another trip.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:51.830
Hey!

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:53.660
You hit me again!

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:57.000
Don't you think it's
Lilith's turn to have some fun?

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:58.230
But-

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.960
But what?

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.230
Then, how about
we travel together?

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:03.500
Sounds good!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:06.060
Two pretty sisters take
off for an unknown journey.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:07.700
Well, well...

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.930
...finally, it seems like peaceful
times will return to this library.

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:18.730
Oh, I tried to wink, but it made
me look like I was falling asleep.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:21.700
My apologies.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:26.830
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:30.930
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:37.560
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:59.960
Yes, finding you means finding myself.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:07.030
I still remember the promise we made.

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:11.000
I've met many people,...

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.860
...and have been
saved so many times.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:18.560
It will all become courage.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:24.200
I'm not alone!

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:29.800
I want to see you,
but I can't see you, if that's a test,...

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:33.300
...then I'll just have to pass it.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:40.760
Don't give in, don't cry,
just wait for me and believe.

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:44.730
I want to see you,
but I can't see you, it hurts so much.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:49.160
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:55.100
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:31.500
I want to see you, but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:34.700
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:42.530
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:22:42.530 --> 00:22:46.460
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:52.460
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:57.330
I'll keep searching for you.

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:39.160
It was nice meeting you.

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:42.160
Please remember me, I'm Hazuki.

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:47.830
For that future day, I will be born...

00:23:47.830 --> 00:23:52.460
...and we will all shine
together around the world.

00:24:03.030 --> 00:24:08.400
Yami, the Hat and
the Book Traveler
